            <ArticleTitle>[Pain: a psychogeriatric perspective].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Identifying pain in old people is very important, because it modifies daily life and functional performance, and it increases dependence from others. It may be expressed not only as a sensitive experience but also as psychological disorders. It interferes with cognitive area and it is a risk factor for suicide. The subject is considered from a multidimensional approach: in the diagnosis of pain in the interview and as a psychiatric evaluation in other medical areas.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
